  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections and Voting in Boone County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n Calendar\n\n Courts\n Elections\n\n Employment\n FAQ\n \n\n Translate Language\n \n Translate\n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n Home\n \n\n Departments \n \n\n 911 Communications\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor\n Board of Supervisors\n Community Services\n Conservation\n Emergency Management\n Engineer/Secondary Roads\n GIS\n Health & Sanitation\n Human Resources\n Information Technology\n Landfill & Recycling\n Planning & Development\n Recorder\n Sheriff\n Treasurer\n Veterans Affairs\n Weed Commissioner\n \n \n \n\n About \n \n\n Cemeteries\n Elected Officials\n Township Information\n \n \n Apply\n Contact\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Clear · 46°\n \n \n\n Find departments, services, staff, and more\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nAuditor\n \n\nElections & Voting\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nWe've compiled everything you need to know about elections and voting, including how & where to vote, finding elected officials, becoming a candidate, and information on past and upcoming elections. Any questions you may have related to elections and voting can be directed to elections@boonecounty.iowa.gov \nVoting and Voter Registration\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Am I Registered?\n \n \n\n \n \n Voting FAQs\n \n \n\n \n \n Register to Vote\n \n \n\n \n \n How to Vote\n \n \n\n \n \n Voting Precincts\n \n \n\n \n \n Absentee Voting\n \n \n\n \n \n Military/Overseas Voting\n \n \n\n \n \n Voter ID\n \n\n\n\n\nElections and Election Results\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Upcoming Elections\n \n \n\n \n \n Election Results\n \n \n\n \n \n Election Types\n \n \n\n \n \n Poll Watching\n \n \n\n \n \n Election Workers\n \n\n\n\n\nOther Information\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Archived Election Results (1966-2023)\n \n \n\n \n \n Candidate Information\n \n \n\n \n \n Elected Officials\n \n \n\n \n \n Election Maps\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n Boone County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated November 1, 2024\n \n\n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n7,937\n \n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n7,258\n \n\n \nDemocrat\n \n\n\n \n5,010\n \n\n \nLibertarian\n \n\n\n \n154\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n23\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 20,382\n \n Register to Vote\n\n \n \n\n \nAuditor\n Drainage\n Drainage On Beacon\n Elections & Voting\n Financial and Tax Information\n Real Estate\n Drainage FAQ\n FAQ\n Department Home\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n Back · Boone County Auditor\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nDid You Know\n \nSign up to receive notifications when board meetings and agendas are posted, job openings are announced, and more.\n Customize Your Notifications\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nMission Statement\n \nThe mission of Boone County is to be accountable to its citizens in providing innovative and high-quality\ngovernment services in an economical, fair, professional, and courteous manner to enhance and protect the\nhealth, welfare, and safety of those who live and work in Boone County.\n\n\n\n \nBoone County, Iowa\n\n 201 State St.\n\nBoone, IA 50036\n\n Contact Us\n \n\n \nCourthouse Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n\n 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.\n\n Closed Holidays\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n©2026 Boone County, Iowa\n \npowered by \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nVeteran’s Day (November 11, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving Day (November 26, 2026)\n \nBlack Friday (November 27, 2026)\n \nChristmas Eve Afternoon (December 24, 2026)\n \nChristmas Day (December 25, 2026)\n \n\n\n\n"
